course: dictionary
lesson: 11659
title: Ascertain: a formal way to say find out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ascertain is a formal word. It means to find out for certain, usually by checking carefully. «The scientist checked the results to ascertain whether the medicine worked.» She checked carefully so she could be sure. Ascertain means find out for certain.
explain: In maths, ascertain often means work out. «Ascertain the total of the bill» is an instruction: find the total. Try swapping in find or work out, and the sentence still makes sense. That swap test is a good check.
explain: In everyday talk, nobody says ascertain. People say «find out», «check», «figure out» (US) or «suss out» (UK and Australia). Using ascertain at home can sound jokey: «I shall ascertain the whereabouts of my socks.»
fact: Ascertain means to find out for certain, usually by checking carefully.
fact: Ascertain is a formal word, used in exams, science, reports and the news.
fact: Common phrases include ascertain whether, ascertain the cause, ascertain how many and ascertain the facts.
fact: «Ascertain» means the same as «find out» or «work out».
fact: In everyday talk, say «find out», «check» or «figure out» (US) instead.
exercise: «The doctor will ascertain whether the bone is broken.» What does ascertain mean here? | *Find out for certain | Forget about it | Break into pieces | Guess quickly and move on
exercise: Exam question: «Ascertain the total of the numbers 4, 5 and 6.» What does the question want you to do? | *Find the total | Count backwards from ten | Sing the numbers | Write the numbers in words
exercise: Which everyday phrase means the same as ascertain? | Look away | Shout loudly | Give up | *Check or find out
test: «Police are trying to ascertain the cause of the fire.» Which word could replace ascertain without changing the meaning much? | *Find out | Ignore | Hide | Celebrate
test: Mum says, «I shall ascertain the whereabouts of my socks.» Why is this funny? | *It uses a stiff, formal word for a simple search at home | It means she is very angry | It is the name of a shop | Socks are never funny
exam: Which sentence uses ascertain correctly? | I ascertain my dinner every night | The dog ascertained loudly in the garden | The bus ascertained to the station | *The team set out to ascertain the facts before they made a decision
